DOOMSDAY COMMUNICATOR – DOCUMENTATION
(Technical description of the protocol, architecture, and operation
of the PicoMesh network – a decentralized LoRa network)
===============================================================

1. INTRODUCTION – SYSTEM PURPOSE AND CONCEPT
---------------------------------------------------------------
In crisis situations—such as infrastructure failures, natural
disasters, power outages, or conflicts—traditional communication
systems may cease to function. Cellular networks, the Internet,
and even local radio networks can become overloaded or destroyed.

The Doomsday Communicator (PicoMesh) was designed as a
decentralized, resilient, and democratic communication network
operating entirely independently of external infrastructure.
Every node is equal; any node can transmit and relay packets,
and the network has no single point of failure.

The system utilizes LoRa (SX1262) to build a lightweight mesh
network in which packets are relayed between nodes using a
flooding method with TTL control. This allows the network to
operate even with a minimal number of nodes, while its topology
can change dynamically without loss of functionality.

The system's objectives are:
- enabling text-based communication in the absence of infrastructure,
- automatic packet relay between nodes,
- broadcasting GPS positions and node status,
- resilience against failures and attacks,
- full decentralization and the absence of central control,
- minimal energy consumption,
- maximum simplicity of implementation. 
