===============================================================
PACKET FORMAT AND PROTOCOL
===============================================================

3. PACKET FORMAT
---------------------------------------------------------------
The packet is text-based, debuggable, and easy to parse:

type|src|dst|mid|ttl|data

Example:
MSG|N001|N005|312|5|Hello, are you there?

Packet types:
- MSG – text message,
- ACK – acknowledgment,
- BEA – beacon with GPS/battery info,
- CMD – control commands.


===============================================================
PACKET PROCESSING – processPacket()
===============================================================

4. processPacket() FUNCTION
---------------------------------------------------------------
void processPacket(String pkt) {
pkt.trim(); 
// ... field parsing ...
if (inCache(src, mid)) return; 
addCache(src, mid); 
updateNode(...); 

if (dst != NODE_ID && ttl > 0) {
ttl--; 
forwardPacket(...); 
return; 
}

if (type == "MSG") { ... }
if (type == "ACK") { ... }
if (type == "BEA") { ... }
if (type == "CMD") { ... }
}

The function performs:
1. Packet validation
2. Anti-duplication
3. nodeList update
4. Packet forwarding
5. MSG/ACK/BEA/CMD handling


===============================================================
ANTI-DUPLICATION – CACHE
===============================================================

5. DUPLICATE CACHE
---------------------------------------------------------------
bool inCache(String src, int mid);
void addCache(String src, int mid);

The cache stores the (src, mid) of recent packets. Objective:
- preventing packet looping,
- limiting network traffic,
- stabilizing mesh flooding.
===============================================================
RETRANSMISSIONS – pendingRetries
===============================================================

6. RETRY MECHANISM
---------------------------------------------------------------
void addPendingRetry(Packet p);
void checkPendingRetries();
void removePendingByMID(int mid);

The mechanism ensures reliability:
- MSG is added to pendingRetries,
- if no ACK arrives → retry,
- retry includes jitter to avoid collisions,
- packet is dropped after MAX_MSG_RETRIES.


===============================================================
TX QUEUE WITH PRIORITIES (1–5)
===============================================================

7. TRANSMISSION PRIORITIES
---------------------------------------------------------------
Priorities:
1. ACK
2. MSG in retry
3. Forward
4. New MSG
5. BEA

Packet selection:
bool selectPacketForTx(Packet &out);

Transmission:
void sendFromQueue() {
Packet p; 
if (!selectPacketForTx(p)) return; 

String pkt = p.type + "|" + p.src + "|" + p.dst + "|" +
String(p.mid) + "|" + String(p.ttl) + "|" + p.data; 

LoRa.beginPacket(); 
LoRa.print(pkt); 
LoRa.endPacket(); 
LoRa.receive();
}


===============================================================
1 Hz SCHEDULER – DETERMINISTIC TX
===============================================================

8. SCHEDULER
---------------------------------------------------------------
static unsigned long lastTx = 0;
if (millis() - lastTx >= 1000) {
sendFromQueue(); 
lastTx = millis();
}

Advantages:
- collision minimization,
- predictable load,
- mesh stability,
- no need for CAD.
