===============================================================
RESILIENCE TO FAILURES AND ATTACKS
===============================================================

13. SYSTEM RESILIENCE
---------------------------------------------------------------
1. No single point of failure
The network is fully decentralized.

2. Censorship resistance
No server → no single point to block.

3. Jamming resistance
LoRa (CSS) is resistant to wideband interference.

4. Node takeover resistance
Compromising a single device does not grant control over the network.

5. Topology failure resilience
Mesh flooding + TTL ensure redundancy.

6. Power failure resilience
Nodes can operate on battery power or solar panels.


===============================================================
SUMMARY
===============================================================

14. SUMMARY
---------------------------------------------------------------
The PicoMesh system is a lightweight, resilient text
communication protocol based on LoRa. Thanks to its simplicity,
deterministic scheduler, TX priorities, retries with
backoff, and full decentralization, the system can operate
without infrastructure, serving as an independent
communication network highly resistant to interference
and attacks.

This is not a toy—it is a real-world crisis communication system.
